{"step_index":159,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:41:15Z","thinking":"**Directly analyzing the graph problem**\n\nThe problem involves a graph $G$ and a Roman dominating function $f$. $f$ maps vertices to values 0, 1, or 2, with $V_0, V_1, V_2$ representing the sets of vertices with those respective values. The weight $w(f)$ is defined as $|V_1| + 2|V_2|$. Now, formulating the plan to prove some property about the Roman dominating function.\n\n\n**Defining a total dominating set**\n\nThe goal is to show the existence of a total dominating set $S$ with a size constraint $|S| \\le |V_1| + 2|V_2|$. A total dominating set requires every vertex in the graph to have a neighbor in the set $S$. The initial strategy involves leveraging the properties of $V_0, V_1, V_2$.\n\nSince $V_2$ dominates $V_0$, focusing on how to extend a set containing $V_2$ to dominate $V_1 \\cup V_2$ is key. Defining $X$ as the subset of $V_1 \\cup V_2$ with no neighbors in $V_2$ seems useful. Now thinking about the budget constraints.\n\n\n**Calculating the set's size**\n\nThe remaining budget after adding $V_2$ is $|V_1| + |V_2|$. The focus shifts to dominating vertices in $X$. Determining the maximum size of $X$ is crucial; it's bounded above by $|V_1| + |V_2|$. Each vertex in $X$ requires just one neighbor in $S$. Defining the candidate set as $S = V_2 \\cup \\{n(u) : u \\in X\\}$ seems correct.\n\nEvery vertex is dominated by the construction of $S$. Verifying the total dominating set property, and then checking the size, $|S|$, confirms the size is exactly $w(f) = |V_1| + 2|V_2|$. The goal seems to be achieved. Re-examining the derivation steps, ensuring no logic is missed.\n\n\n**Verifying the size of the set**\n\nSince $X$ is defined as vertices without neighbors in $V_2$, $X$ must be a subset of $V_1 \\cup V_0$. Because the Roman dominating function implies that vertices in $V_0$ must have neighbors in $V_2$, no vertex in $V_0$ can be in $X$, therefore $X$ is a subset of $V_1$. $|X| \\le |V_1|$.\n\nConstructing $S$ involved adding neighbors for each vertex in $X$. Since for any $u \\in X$, $g(u)$ is adjacent to $u$. Then, $|S| = |V_2| + |\\{g(u) : u \\in X\\}|$. Using the definition of $X$, and $V_2$ is disjoint from $V_1$, the size of S is at most $|V_2| + |V_1|$. This corresponds exactly to the definition of roman weight. This implies $|S| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nimport itertools\n\ndef test():\n    for n in range(2, 9):\n        print(f'Testing n={n}...')\n        for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n            if G.number_of_nodes() != n or any(G.degree(v) == 0 for v in G.nodes()):\n                continue\n            nodes = list(G.nodes())\n            # For each Roman dominating function\n            for f_tup in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n                f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tup))\n                if not all(f[v] > 0 or any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\n                    continue\n                # Weight\n                w = sum(f_tup)\n                V2 = set(v for v in nodes if f[v] == 2)\n                V1 = set(v for v in nodes if f[v] == 1)\n                # X: vertices with no neighbor in V2\n                X = [v for v in nodes if not any(u in V2 for u in G.neighbors(v))]\n                # verify X is subset of V1 cup V2\n                assert all(v in V1 or v in V2 for v in X)\n                # choose one neighbor for each v in X\n                chosen_neighbors = set(next(iter(G.neighbors(v))) for v in X)\n                S = V2.union(chosen_neighbors)\n                # verify S is total dominating set\n                for v in nodes:\n                    assert any(u in S for u in G.neighbors(v))\n                # verify |S| <= w\n                assert len(S) <= w\n\ntest()\nprint('ALL TESTS PASSED!')\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Verifying the proof algorithm on all graphs up to order 7","toolSummary":"Verify proof algorithm"}}]}
{"step_index":160,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:41:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:41:24+02:00\nTool is running as a background task with task id: b7d4c44b-5d24-4df7-a810-6c80a370a2fc/task-160\nTask Description: /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nimport itertools\n\ndef test():\n    for n in range(2, 9):\n        print(f'Testing n={n}...')\n        for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n            if G.number_of_nodes() != n or any(G.degree(v) == 0 for v in G.nodes()):\n                continue\n            nodes = list(G.nodes())\n            # For each Roman dominating function\n            for f_tup in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n                f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tup))\n                if not all(f[v] > 0 or any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\n                    continue\n                # Weight\n                w = sum(f_tup)\n                V2 = set(v for v in nodes if f[v] == 2)\n                V1 = set(v for v in nodes if f[v] == 1)\n                # X: vertices with no neighbor in V2\n                X = [v for v in nodes if not any(u in V2 for u in G.neighbors(v))]\n                # verify X is subset of V1 cup V2\n                assert all(v in V1 or v in V2 for v in X)\n                # choose one neighbor for each v in X\n                chosen_neighbors = set(next(iter(G.neighbors(v))) for v in X)\n                S = V2.union(chosen_neighbors)\n                # verify S is total dominating set\n                for v in nodes:\n                    assert any(u in S for u in G.neighbors(v))\n                # verify |S| <= w\n                assert len(S) <= w\n\ntest()\nprint('ALL TESTS PASSED!')\n\"\nTask logs are available at: file:///tmp/agyhome.XMOFQj/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/b7d4c44b-5d24-4df7-a810-6c80a370a2fc/.system_generated/tasks/task-160.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO A