{"step_index":167,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:41:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:41:41+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:41:41+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 30 to 70\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n30: namespace GraphCalc\n31: \n32: variable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n33: \n34: /-- Least cardinality of a subset satisfying `p`, or `0` when none does.\n35: \n36: The `0` fallback is only harmless when *some* subset satisfies `p` — for\n37: `indepNum`, `dominationNumber` and `vertexCoverNumber`, `univ` always does. It\n38: is NOT harmless in general, and treating it as such produced a real defect:\n39: `IsConnectedZeroForcingSet` is unsatisfiable on a disconnected graph (`univ`\n40: does not induce a connected subgraph), so the invariant silently read `0` where\n41: graphcalc reports \"undefined\". A conjecture `Z_c + 2 ≤ 2 * Z_t` then became\n42: `2 ≤ 0` and was refutable with no mathematical content.\n43: \n44: Any new invariant built on `minCard` must either prove `univ` satisfies its\n45: predicate, or expose a `Has…` witness predicate below and be exported under it. -/\n46: def minCard (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n47:   ((univ.powerset.filter p).image Finset.card).min.getD 0\n48: \n49: /-- Some subset satisfies `p`: exactly the precondition `minCard` needs for its\n50: value to mean \"the least cardinality\" rather than \"there were none\". -/\n51: def HasWitness (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : Prop :=\n52:   ∃ s ∈ (univ : Finset V).powerset, p s\n53: \n54: instance (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : Decidable (HasWitness p) := by\n55:   unfold HasWitness; infer_instance\n56: \n57: /-- Greatest `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `0` when none does. -/\n58: def maxUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n59:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).max).getD 0\n60: \n61: /-- Least `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `n` when none does. -/\n62: def minUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n63:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).min).getD n\n64: \n65: /- ── order / size ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n66: \n67: def order (_G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ := Fintype.card V\n68: \n69: def size (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ := G.edgeFinset.card\n70: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":168,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:41:41Z","thinking":"**Comparing `minCard` and `romanDominationNumber`**\n\nThe `minCard` function computes the minimum cardinality of sets satisfying a predicate `p` from all subsets of a universal set. `romanDominationNumber` calculates the minimum \"roman weight\" of functions that are roman dominating for a given graph. Both functions use a similar pattern of filtering a set (powersets or functions in the respective cases), mapping the filtered set to a numerical value (cardinality or roman weight), and then taking the minimum of the numerical results. `univ` is a set of functions from vertices to `Fin 3`. The `getD 0` ensures a default value if the minimum is not defined, but the sets should not be empty, so no effect.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity_handoff.py","EndLine":150,"StartLine":80,"toolAction":"Viewing antigravity_handoff.py lint rules","toolSummary":"View lint rules"}}]}
