{"step_index":192,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:42:38Z","thinking":"**Planning `Candidate` Proof**\n\nThe test script completed successfully, so the focus shifts to planning the Lean 4 proof. Reviewing the `Candidate` definition, the goal is to prove an inequality involving total and Roman domination numbers for simple graphs. The proof will involve universal quantifiers over types, finite types, decidable equality, simple graphs, and decidable adjacency relations. It depends on several graph properties and inequality.\n\n\n**Decomposing Assumptions and Definitions**\n\nFocusing on the provided assumptions and definitions within the Lean context. The assumption `h_has_td` implies the existence of a total dominating set for the graph. This further implies that no vertex is isolated, deriving the `no_isolated` lemma. The roman domination number is defined as the minimum weight of all Roman dominating functions, derived from the `univ` set. Checking if the `Finset ℕ` is nonempty, finding out that the constant function satisfies the `RomanDominationFunction` requirement.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\n#check Finset.min\n#check Finset.min_eq_some_iff\n#check Finset.min_le_of_mem\n#check Option.getD\n","Description":"Checking Finset.min lemmas in scratch_test.lean","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333/scratch_test.lean","toolAction":"Writing lemmas check in scratch_test.lean","toolSummary":"Check Finset.min lemmas"}}]}
